\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Every exported construction has explicit input hypotheses, an output specification, its relevant invariance theorem, and any required fibrancy theorem. There is no blanket fixed-target rectification theorem. A comparison may replace a model by an equivalent strict model; strict maps into the original model are a stronger, separately stated claim. No \code{hP} truncation is assumed for arbitrary roots.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{A named future theorem is not evidence that its hypotheses hold.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{A universal closure checklist whose individual entries have not been formulated; silently using levelwise invariance as categorical invariance.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-fd-0005}, \ref{at-fd-0006}, \ref{at-fd-0008}, \ref{at-fd-0010}.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{frozen export policy; mathematical instances provisional until proved.}
}
